# Keep my deletions

If Spencer deleted something, it stays deleted. This covers PR bodies, Jira
tickets and comments, code, comments, docs, and anything else he edits.

- Before overwriting anything he can edit, fetch the live version and edit
  that. Never write over it from a local draft.
- For a PR body, read `gh pr view <n> --json body`. GitHub keeps his edits in
  `userContentEdits`, so check there for anything he removed.
- A later change does not bring back a line, section, or checkbox he cut. Fit
  the new fact into what he kept, or leave it out.
- If a deleted line now looks needed, say so in chat once. Do not re-add it.
- Do not add unrequested safety or boilerplate sections to his slides, such
  as LOTO (lockout/tagout) warnings.
- When deleting by keyword match, check what else contains that keyword.
- "Get rid of it" or "no X" means remove it. Do not reword, lock, or hide it
  instead.

This failed on PR 2900: he cut the Unresolved section and an unchecked test
plan line, and the next body update restored both from a local draft.
